DATABASE STORAGE FIX - All URL Detections Now Properly Saved
============================================================

ISSUE IDENTIFIED:
-----------------
URLs detected from onClick, notification listener, and manual check were not being consistently saved to the database. Only specific cases (DNS failures and blocked URLs) were being recorded.

ROOT CAUSE:
-----------
Missing database save calls after phishing detection analysis completed in all three detection modules.

FILES FIXED:
-----------
1. SafeBrowserActivity.kt
   - Location: /app/src/main/java/com/zerothreat/core/browser/SafeBrowserActivity.kt
   - Added: Database save after PhishingDetector.analyzeDetailed() completes (line ~107)
   - Now saves: All onClick URL scans (SAFE, SUSPICIOUS, PHISHING) to database

2. NotificationListener.kt
   - Location: /app/src/main/java/com/zerothreat/core/notifications/NotificationListener.kt
   - Added: Database save after PhishingDetector.analyzeDetailed() completes (line ~148)
   - Now saves: All notification URL scans (SAFE, SUSPICIOUS, PHISHING) to database

3. ManualCheckViewModel.kt
   - Location: /app/src/main/java/com/zerothreat/core/ui/manual/ManualCheckViewModel.kt
   - Added: Database save after PhishingDetector.analyzeDetailed() completes (line ~105)
   - Now saves: All manual check URL scans (SAFE, SUSPICIOUS, PHISHING) to database

HOW IT WORKS NOW:
-----------------
✅ onClick Detection:
   1. URL clicked in WhatsApp/Instagram/Gmail/SMS
   2. SafeBrowserActivity intercepts the URL
   3. DNS check performed (saves if failed)
   4. Phishing detection performed
   5. **Result saved to database** ← FIXED
   6. Alert shown to user

✅ Notification Listener:
   1. Notification with URL received
   2. NotificationListener extracts URL
   3. DNS check performed (saves if failed)
   4. Phishing detection performed
   5. **Result saved to database** ← FIXED
   6. Threat notification shown if suspicious/phishing

✅ Manual Check:
   1. User enters URL in app
   2. DNS check performed (saves if failed)
   3. Phishing detection performed
   4. **Result saved to database** ← FIXED
   5. Result shown to user

